2. The "Trust & Verification" Tier (Security Focus)
Since you mentioned security is a priority, use the subscription to fund the verification process.
The Perk: A "Background Verified" Badge
Focusing subscriptions exclusively on the Handyman (the service provider) is a smart business move. It keeps the barrier to entry low for clients, ensuring a high volume of jobs, while the professionals pay for the "privilege" of accessing those leads.

Since you want the clients to feel secure and the handymen to find value beyond just a price reduction, here are several subscription ideas tailored for the Handyman in your app:

1. The "Trust & Verification" Tier (Security Focus)
Since you mentioned security is a priority, use the subscription to fund the verification process.

The Perk: A "Background Verified" Badge.

How it works: Handymen who subscribe get their identity documents (ID cards, certifications) manually reviewed by you.

Why it works: Clients are much more likely to hire someone with a "Verified" badge. The subscription covers the "cost of trust."

2. The "Lead Priority" (The Head-Start)
In a busy market, being first is everything.
The Perk: Early Access to Jobs.
How it works: When a client posts a job, Subscribed Handymen see it and can bid on it 30 minutes to 1 hour before "Free" handymen.
Why it works: High-paying or urgent jobs will be snapped up by subscribers before the free users even see the notification.

3. Visibility & "The Spotlight"
The Perk: Search Boost.

How it works: When a client searches for a "Plumber" or "Electrician," subscribed pros appear at the very top of the list.

Why it works: Most users don't scroll past the first 5 results. Being #1 significantly increases their monthly income.

4. Professional Business Tools
Turn your app into a "Mini-Office" for the handyman.

The Perk: Advanced Portfolio & Analytics.

How it works:

Unlimited Photos: Free users can show 3 photos of their work; Subscribers can upload a full gallery.

Invoice Generator: Allow them to generate professional PDF receipts for clients directly in the app.

Monthly Stats: Show them a chart of how many people viewed their profile vs. how many hired them.

